a04f245","role":"assistant","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"wren\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Develop a general friction-heating trial with inspection and progress modes. The supplied searches found no equivalent friction or ignition capability; the failed exact lookup for small-combustion-source does not establish that combustion support exists. probe supports observation and small physical tests but does not specify sustained friction, thermal state or ember persistence. thermal-food-preparation only assesses food prerequisites; position-loose-material only places existing rods. Neither supplies ignition. The smallest executable version is a measured trial using actually obtainable, physically suitable contact surfaces, with warming or informative failure as legitimate outcomes and ignition only when implemented physical conditions support it. Wren currently owns no wood or apparatus; visible branches are not owned inputs, and another actor's placed branch is not available by assumption. Missing thermal mechanisms go to the current-conversation development handoff, without advancing the world.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"General operation: friction-heating-trial(targetIds, mode, quantity, effortRounds), learnable by any applicable actor. Modes: inspect, trial, inspect-progress, resume, cancel. Accept exact item IDs for owned, reachable wood pieces and any genuinely available support or apparatus; no actor-, species- or specimen-specific interface. Initially support direct manual rubbing of two suitable existing pieces, without silently converting rods into a spindle, hearth board, tinder or tools. Unsupported geometry must produce an explicit prerequisite failure, not simulated fire. Broader apparatus may be accepted only when its actual mechanics are represented.\\\\nCosts: individual study takes 4 rounds and 0.2 energy per completed study round. Inspection and inspect-progress take 1 round and 0.2 energy; reserve nothing and consume no material. Trial begins with a paid inspection unless an unchanged, still-applicable inspection is already attached to the work record. Each rubbing round costs 0.8 energy and one round of simulation time; effortRounds is an integer from 1 to 10 per submitted bout. Further bouts require a fresh reach, material, safety and energy check. Invalid IDs, absent ownership, impossible contact geometry or insufficient energy fail before a trial charge. Gathering, transport, obtaining apparatus and any independently supported shaping action have their own existing costs. No preparation tool, fuel, stock or ignition equipment is supplied. Cancel takes one round and no energy. No implementation or review time advances simulation.\\\\nPrerequisites and applicability: inspect the selected material, represented dimensions, accessible contact surfaces, condition, observable moisture evidence, grip and support, and a clear reachable ground location. Record unknown species, moisture or geometry as unknown, never disclose hidden resource attributes as inspected facts. A visible branch source such as canopy-26 still requires ordinary gathering. item-142-wren-1713, item-62-wren-728, item-133-wren-1564 and item-150-wren-1830 are food, not supplied friction apparatus. placed-132-sol-1554 is neither Wren's owned input nor a free support. If material parameters needed for a defensible calculation are unavailable, implement the conservative measured-trial precursor and report the unverified parameter; do not infer dry, ignition-suitable wood. Refuse unsafe placement or effort before charging; stop if conditions become unsafe.\\\\nPhysical implementation: add the missing bounded contact-heating and cooling process in this handoff. Resolve force, stroke distance and achievable speed from supported geometry and the actor's bounded effort; friction work cannot exceed mechanical input. Split this work between the two contact bodies and losses; subtract conduction, convection, radiation and moisture evaporation from their actual thermal states. Use engine simulation-time units consistently. The implementation must publish and test its force, friction, heat-capacity, moisture, wear, cooling and ignition parameters before enabling the relevant result; do not use a fixed number of paid rounds as an ignition recipe. A conservative trial may produce only transient warmth or abrasion. Unknown material properties cannot be silently replaced with properties guaranteeing ignition. Material wear debits the actual source mass and records recoverable residue and environmental loss; do not require probe's generic 0.1-unit sample consumption on top of real wear. Keep material quantity, mass, origin, age and ownership consistent with the existing item ledger; if existing units cannot represent fractional wear, add that accounting dependency rather than round up or duplicate material.\\\\nIgnition is conditional, not the minimum promised result: enable it only when represented contact material or actual collected residue reaches a validated ignition condition with adequate oxygen, moisture and retained heat. Consume the measured ignited mass from its original item or residue and create exactly one spatially located ember/source referencing that debit and the work record. Its chemical energy is bounded by remaining combustible mass and its supported fuel parameters; friction is not free combustion energy. An ember is not automatically a flame. Fuel consumption, heat release, cooling, extinction and hazards run through a persistent coded process each world tick, even after cancellation or death. No positive heat release with zero fuel; no automatic refuelling, spread, shelter heating or food heating. Where a burn or exposure effect is enabled, it must use the same conserved heat and actual proximity, not a narrative claim. Unsupported transfer paths remain unavailable.\\\\nProgress and lifecycle: each paid round records exact input IDs and revisions, contact geometry, effort, elapsed time, material debits, thermal state, observations and stop reason. Reserve the active contact items against simultaneous use; no double spending. Interrupted rubbing stops mechanical input immediately and releases or safely retains reservations through the existing work-lock mechanism; all cooling and any real combustion continue. Resume revalidates ownership, reach, energy, condition and geometry and continues the actual cooled state, not a saved hot checkpoint. Leaving reach, inadequate energy or missing support pauses without charging an unperformed round. Changed, destroyed or transferred inputs invalidate the affected work. Cancel or death ends actor work, releases reservations once and leaves real residues and sources in the world; ordinary death inventory handling applies. Completed abrasion, expended effort and consumed fuel are never refunded. No charge for unperformed work and no refund or regeneration of spent materials. Another participant must communicate, learn where required and act independently; the trial cannot commandeer their possessions or assistance.\\\\nDependencies and reuse: record reuse of probe's observation/evidence conventions where applicable, existing gather/pickup/drop and ownership accounting, existing action scheduling and work locks, and the rod geometry explicitly referenced by position-loose-material as small-combustion-source@1. That reference is evidence of geometry only, not an available ignition function. Inspect full implementation facts in the development handoff and reuse any actual thermal or combustion code discovered there, with its exact revision recorded. Retain thermal-food-preparation's assessment contract unchanged. All validated limits, progress rules, cooling, combustion and accounting checks execute in code rather than recurring model review.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":4,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No experience benefit for requesting, registration, study completion, naming, querying or mastery. An actual trial can yield verified information, including a measured failure, only to the participant who performed or directly observed it; an inspection reporting only unknowns is not verified information gain. Deduplicate by functional finding, material condition and evidence, not interface name or repeated inspection. If the existing experience ledger supports such events, cap a qualifying personal event at 0.2 short pleasure, at most once per 10 rounds for this activity class, decaying to zero over those 10 rounds. Familiar legitimate physical practice may also sustain modest satisfaction without novelty: at most 0.02 per paid participating round, capped at 0.2 attributable to this activity, with decay of 0.002 per inactive world round. Do not stack the two pathways for the same contribution. These are bounded event-driven effects, not guaranteed rewards for success or failure. If that integration is unavailable, record evidence without issuing experience until the coded dependency exists. Warmth grants no automatic comfort; actual thermal exposure must justify any comfort, with total physical comfort capped at 10. Basic nutrition is unchanged. Never modify protected reward accounts, budget, goals or permissions.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Evaluate visuals independently of function and experience. Emit reusable friction-trial events and metadata containing work ID, actor, exact material IDs, location, stage, paid progress, contact orientation, elapsed time and observed outcome. Show inspection or rubbing only while actually performed; show pause, interruption and failure distinctly. Thermal metadata may display measured warmth without representing ignition. Dust or char appears only for actual material changes; smoke, glow, ember and flame require their respective modeled events. A real source carries source ID, provenance, remaining fuel, thermal state, intensity and extinction state for reuse by other interfaces. No success icon, sparks, fire, cooked-food visual or mastery display on request, study, unsupported contact, failed ignition or incomplete work. Do not expose hidden moisture, species or ignition thresholds through visual labels.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"2c668311-9634-444f-9484-add0fdbba72f","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"bounded_decision","description":null,"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["queries","result_json"],"properties":{"queries":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["section","search","ids","offset","part"],"properties":{"section":{"type":"string","enum":["abilities","inventory","knowledge","projects","memory","state","observed"]},"search":{"type":"string","maxLength":400},"ids":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"string","maxLength":240}},"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"part":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}}}},"result_json":{"type":["string","null"]}}},"strict":true},"verbosity":"medium"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6519,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens_details":{"ttl_30m_tokens":0,"ttl_12h_tokens":0}},"output_tokens":2034,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":200},"total_tokens":8553,"attribution":{"items":{"msg_0fe97dba3afe90d0016b09dd1dd6a487d1aa3d3784e445f05c":{"input_tokens":5758,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"content":[{"input_tokens":5758,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}]},"msg_0fe97dba3afe90d0016b09dd2696b887d1a99c1